 "verdict": {
  "mechanism": "GEOMETRY SWITCH (human_k=6), not entropy collapse and not speed overshoot. The policy is a line-overfitted pure-pursuit follower: each checkpoint only completes the route on the exact path geometry its lookahead observations were trained on. race_v8 (trained on 6 human tracks) arrives 77-100 % on 4 of those 6 tracks (mean 76.7 %, matching its training log's 77-80 %) but 0/48 on the navmesh env the strict protocol builds; symmetrically race_v7 (trained on the navmesh plan) arrives 89.6 % there but 0/48 on human track geometry. On the navmesh env every v8 episode executes the first 2.3 s (west-wall climb to z=118) then leaves the line at the same NW corner turn (x -863..-872, y 630-720, t 2.30-2.64 s, 187-360 ups), falls off the ramp's inner edge and never regains z>=120: 5/8 grind the x=-688 wall on the lower floor at ~330 ups (explains scrape 60-69 % vs corpus band 22 %), 3/8 sit stuck at x=-872 at ~20 ups.",
  "entropy_collapse_rejected": "v8's discrete-head entropies are HIGHER than v7's (fwd 0.216 vs 0.067, side 0.379 vs 0.181 nats on each policy's own visited states); the log's ent -0.93 vs v7's -1.10 is dominated by the yaw log_std; and v8 fails greedy too (0/48), so the decode rule is not the mechanism. Separate pre-existing fragility found: v7 GREEDY from spawn a is a deterministic stall at (-800,153,19) at 18 ups, 0/48 - only sampling saved v7's 89.6 %.",
  "speed_overshoot_rejected": "v8 is SLOWER than v7 on the nav env (median moving speed 344-350 vs 440-443 ups); the scrape explosion is wall-grinding while off-route, not higher speed on the line.",
  "training_vs_strict_discrepancy": "Both numbers are true of different environments: race.py's logged arrival % is measured on the human-path envs (plus 35 % mid-route human-state restarts); strict_eval always constructs the navmesh env. Same decode (sampled), different Route.path geometry.",
  "sngspawn_b_extra_defect": "_REGISTRY_OF maps both sngspawn_a_to_mega and sngspawn_b_to_mega to registry 'sngspawn-to-mega', whose 24 tracks ALL start at spawn a (-880,-232,-16). race_v8 therefore never trained a single episode from spawn b; its training-log 'sngspa b 80 %' was measured on spawn-a geometry."
 },
 "race_v9_fix": [
  "1. Mixed geometry per route: keep the human_k tracks AND the navmesh env in the same Roller batch (e.g. 6 human envs + 1 navmesh env per route), so the eval geometry is in-distribution and the policy must become path-general instead of line-overfitted.",
  "2. Fix _REGISTRY_OF / human_paths_for so sngspawn_b_to_mega gets tracks that start at spawn b (filter registry tracks by start point, or fall back to navmesh for b).",
  "3. Add a periodic strict-style probe during training: every N iters, run sampled episodes on the NAVMESH env from the route start and log that arrival rate next to the rollout number - the two curves diverging is exactly the signal that was missed here.",
  "4. Not recommended: entropy floor (entropy did not collapse) or lower speed weight (v8 is already slower than v7)."
 ]
}